{
  "uid": "kubernetes-south",
  "title": "Kubernetes (south)",
  "description": "The cluster AWX runs on. Cluster object state from kube-state-metrics plus etcd's own metrics. Read the note at the bottom for what is still missing -- notably actual CPU and memory consumption, which needs a bearer token.",
  "tags": [
    "managed-by-git",
    "south",
    "kubernetes"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "editable": false,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Nodes Ready",
      "description": "From kube-state-metrics, which reads the API. A node can be NotReady while every etcd panel below stays green -- that combination is exactly what this dashboard could not show before 2026-08-23.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count(kube_node_status_condition{condition=\"Ready\",status=\"true\"} == 1)"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Pods not Running",
      "description": "Pending, Failed or Unknown. Pending usually means unschedulable -- no node with room, or a taint nothing tolerates. Zero is the expected reading.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count(kube_pod_status_phase{phase!=\"Running\",phase!=\"Succeeded\"} == 1) or vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Container restarts (24h)",
      "description": "A crash-looping container is invisible in etcd metrics and invisible in `kubectl get pods` if it recovers between looks. AWX's own web pod has restarted 23 times historically, all of it before 2026-04-30 -- which only became knowable once this existed.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "round(sum(increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total[24h])) or vector(0))"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 10
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Deployments below desired",
      "description": "Desired versus available replicas. This is the panel that would have shown AWX degraded while its pods still reported Running.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count(kube_deployment_status_replicas_available < kube_deployment_spec_replicas) or vector(0)"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "etcd reachable",
      "description": "Scraped from 127.0.0.1:2381 on the control-plane node, which needs no credentials. etcd is the component whose failure is hardest to attribute afterwards: a slow etcd presents as a slow API server, which presents as everything being slow.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "up{job=\"etcd\"}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "UP",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Has a leader",
      "description": "etcd_server_has_leader. A cluster without a leader accepts no writes, which means the Kubernetes API accepts no changes \u2014 the whole control plane is read-only until this recovers.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "etcd_server_has_leader"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "NO LEADER",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "yes",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Leader changes (6h)",
      "description": "Occasional changes are normal. A rising count means the cluster is churning \u2014 usually disk latency or a starved CPU, both of which are visible on the Management plane dashboard.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "increase(etcd_server_leader_changes_seen_total[6h])"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 4
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "DB size",
      "description": "etcd has a hard quota (2GB by default). Crossing it puts the cluster into a read-only alarm state, and the recovery is a compaction and defrag, not a restart.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "etcd_mvcc_db_total_size_in_bytes"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1073741824
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1932735283
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Disk sync latency (p99)",
      "description": "The single best predictor of etcd trouble. WAL fsync above ~10ms sustained means the disk cannot keep up, and everything above it in the stack starts timing out in ways that look like application faults.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(etcd_disk_wal_fsync_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "WAL fsync p99"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(etcd_disk_backend_commit_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "backend commit p99"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "line"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.01
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Proposals",
      "description": "Failed proposals mean writes were rejected \u2014 usually a leader election in progress or a quorum problem. Pending climbing means etcd is falling behind.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 11
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "rate(etcd_server_proposals_committed_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "committed/s"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "rate(etcd_server_proposals_failed_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "failed/s"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "etcd_server_proposals_pending",
          "legendFormat": "pending"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 5
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Keys and watchers",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "etcd_debugging_mvcc_keys_total",
          "legendFormat": "keys"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "etcd_debugging_mvcc_watcher_total",
          "legendFormat": "watchers"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "lineWidth": 2
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "gRPC traffic",
      "description": "Request rate by method. Uses grpc_server_started_total rather than handled_total: the latter carries a grpc_code label and cost 731 series from a single etcd, half the whole etcd budget, so it is dropped at scrape time. The loss is per-code error breakdown \u2014 visible instead as failed proposals in the panel above.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 19
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (grpc_method) (rate(grpc_server_started_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{grpc_method}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 5
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Pods by phase",
      "description": "Watch for a rising Pending line: it means the scheduler cannot place work, which presents to a user as 'nothing is happening' rather than as an error.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (phase) (kube_pod_status_phase == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "{{phase}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Container restarts by pod",
      "description": "Only pods that have actually restarted appear. A single step is a one-off; a staircase is a crash loop.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 26
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (namespace, pod) (increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total[1h])) > 0",
          "legendFormat": "{{namespace}}/{{pod}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 5
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard still cannot tell you",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**kube-state-metrics is deployed** (2026-08-23), so node conditions, pod phases, restart counts and deployment replicas are real above. The `infra-observability` ServiceAccount that unblocked it is **granted and in use** \u2014 read-only, `get/list/watch` on eight resource kinds, no write verb anywhere.\n\nIt is scraped over a NodePort on loopback from the control-plane node only, so **nothing outside the cluster holds a kubeconfig or a token**: the RBAC is consumed by kube-state-metrics itself. The `instance` label is the *cluster*, not the host that scraped it \u2014 these are cluster facts, and labelling them per-host would read as something they are not.\n\n**Still missing, and what each would need:**\n\n| missing | needs |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| API server latency, request rates, error codes | a bearer token on the scraper |\n| kubelet / cAdvisor \u2014 actual CPU and memory *used* per pod | a bearer token on the scraper |\n| scheduler and controller-manager | a bearer token on the scraper |\n\nThat distinction matters: kube-state-metrics reports what the API **says** \u2014 desired replicas, phases, conditions. It does not report **consumption**. A pod at its memory limit looks perfectly healthy here right up until it is OOMKilled, and then appears only as a restart count.\n\n**There is deliberately no API server panel.** `/healthz` answers anonymously but returns the string `ok`, not Prometheus format, so scraping it produced `up{job=\"kube-apiserver\"} = 0` forever \u2014 a permanent zero indistinguishable from a dead control plane."
      }
    }
  ]
}